questions.questionText:
Let ℝ^{3} be a topological space with the usual topology and ℚ denote the set of rational numbers. Define the subspaces 𝑋, 𝑌, 𝑍 and 𝑊 of ℝ^{3} as follows:

𝑋= {(𝑥, 𝑦, 𝑧) \in ℝ^{3} ∶ |𝑥| + |𝑦| + |𝑧| \in ℚ} 𝑌= {(𝑥, 𝑦, 𝑧) \in ℝ^{3} ∶ 𝑥𝑦𝑧= 1} 𝑍= {(𝑥, 𝑦, 𝑧) \in ℝ^{3} ∶ 𝑥^{2} + 𝑦^{2} + 𝑧^{2} = 1} 𝑊= {(𝑥, 𝑦, 𝑧) \in ℝ^{3} ∶ 𝑥𝑦𝑧= 0 }

Which of the following statements is correct?

